text:
A rule~$R$,
\[
\AxiomC{$S_1$}
\AxiomC{$\dots$}
\AxiomC{$S_n$}
\RightLabel{$R$}
\TrinaryInfC{$S$}
\DisplayProof
\]
is called \emph{derivable} in a system if there is a schematic
!!{proof} of the sequent~$S$ using the rules and axioms of the system
together with additional initial sequents of the forms of~$S_1$, \dots,~$S_n$.
